cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its evaluation harnesses, please cite it as below."
title: "ESGenuine: claim-level extraction and integrity auditing of corporate ESG reports"
abstract: >-
  ESGenuine parses corporate ESG and sustainability reports into individually
  auditable claims, normalises them against an ESG taxonomy, and scores document
  integrity from greenwashing-signal flags, cross-report contradictions, external
  fact-checks and Sentinel-2 satellite evidence. The repository additionally ships
  offline evaluation harnesses for extraction precision, mechanically-derived table
  recall, a deterministic-stack ablation, and external baselines.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/iamnishaant/ESGenuine"
version: "4.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-10"

authors:
  - family-names: Bajpai
    given-names: Ansh
    email: anshbajpai2005@gmail.com
    # affiliation: ""
    # orcid: ""

keywords:
  - ESG
  - greenwashing detection
  - claim extraction
  - information extraction
  - climate NLP
  - document AI
  - sustainability reporting

# ── Reproducibility notes for anyone citing a NUMBER from this repository ─────────────
#
# Read `backend/tests/eval/README.md` before quoting any figure. In short:
#
#   * The headline `precision_composite` (Tata 96.1 / Shell 89.7) is PRECISION-FAMILY
#     with no recall term, computed on DEVELOPMENT sets. Neither set is held out — the
#     ontology was tuned against both. They are not evidence of generalization.
#   * Measured table-fact recall on the same pipeline and document is far lower
#     (Tata 54.0% for the shipped configuration; 59.5% before the repair layer).
#     Quote precision and recall together or neither.
#   * All 146 gold labels are single-annotator with no agreement statistic.
#   * Local model weights are pinned by commit SHA and RNGs seeded (`src/model_config.py`),
#     so the ablation, recall and baseline harnesses reproduce exactly and offline.
#     The LLM extraction stage is NOT reproducible: it calls hosted models at
#     temperature 0.1. Results depending on it are reproducible only via the frozen
#     fixtures committed under `backend/tests/eval/fixtures/`.
#
# The gold sets are keyed to extractor output rather than source text; the replacement
# protocol is specified in `docs/ANNOTATION_PROTOCOL.md`.
